   <media:description>Gen AI is ushering in an entirely new era in education. But so what? 
Is learning by heart outdated? Does AI force teachers to innovate? Do professors wish they were students today?

We asked Nako Nakatsuka, an assistant professor at EPFL’s Chemical Nanotechnology Laboratory, and Francesco Mondada, academic director of the Center for Learning Sciences at EPFL, to weigh in.

Want to explore the topic further? Check out our online report &quot;AI takes root in university curriculum&quot;: https://epfl.shorthandstories.com/backtoschool26/index.html

